Symbols Nerd Font Mono, Nerd Fonts 3.5.1. Not a Font list entry: bateri draws
private-use-area symbols (git branch, folder, Powerline) from it when the
selected font has none.

Unmodified copy of the single-width ("Mono") build of the Symbols Only font:
a glyph one cell wide fits one cell.

- `SymbolsNerdFontMono-Regular.ttf`: NerdFontsSymbolsOnly.zip of the GitHub
  release v3.5.1, https://github.com/ryanoasis/nerd-fonts/releases/tag/v3.5.1
  (sha256 fdca3682534f6f65e1ccb2345b0362ccf67d9b8eca7c8025330946e93e2473bc)
  sha256 fe471e538392f51910faab985fa8e192a39dd3426125edd15b71b3680df0e749.
- `LICENSE`: MIT (the Nerd Fonts project), from the same archive.

The font combines icon sets that keep their own licenses (Nerd Fonts'
README for the release lists them):

  Codicons 0.0.45 (Microsoft)           CC BY 4.0
  Devicons 2.17.0                        MIT
  extraglyphs (Hack)                     MIT
  Font Awesome 6.5.1                     CC BY 4.0
  Font Awesome Extension 0.0.3           MIT
  Font Logos 1.3.0                       Unlicense (public domain)
  Material Design Icons (Oct 6, 2022)    Apache-2.0
  Octicons 18.3.0                        MIT
  Seti-UI and original                   MIT
  Pomicons 1.001                         OFL 1.1
  Powerline Extra Symbols 1.200          MIT
  Powerline Symbols                      MIT
  Power Symbols (IEC)                    MIT
  Weather Icons 2.0.10                   OFL 1.1

Attribution for the CC BY 4.0 sets (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/)
is in the bundle's THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.txt.
